Runtest for fsm blocks in .comp files (docs/dev/MODCOMPILE_FSM_DESIGN.md): an internal on, 'on (cond) { action }' without a target, runs its action and stays in the state (no on_exit/on_enter, the timer runs on); as the match of the run it holds back the on items after it and the timeout, which fires as soon as the internal on no longer matches if it is overdue; not run while the fsm is disabled. A second fsm has an internal timeout, timeout (t) { action }: a level like an internal on, after the on items, the timer running on.
